              "content": "# MySQL Query Panel Configuration Guide\n\n## Overview\nThis dashboard demonstrates how to create and configure panels with MySQL queries using the OpenEdX MySQL datasource. Below you'll find a sample panel with a pre-configured query that you can use as a reference for creating your own panels.\n\n## How to Create a MySQL Query Panel\n1. Click the \"Add panel\" button in your dashboard\n\n2. Select \"Add a new panel\"\n\n3. In the query editor, select the \"Openedx MySQL\" datasource\n\n4. Write your SQL query in the query editor. For example:\n```sql\nSELECT u.id, u.username, u.email, u.is_active \nFROM auth_user u \nLIMIT 100\n```\n\n5. Configure the visualization type (Table, Graph, etc.) based on your data\n\n## Example Panel\nBelow you'll find a sample panel that queries the `auth_user` table. This example shows:\n- Basic user information\n- How to structure a simple SELECT query\n- How to limit results\n\n## Tips for Writing MySQL Queries\n- Always use appropriate indexes for better performance\n- Limit the number of rows returned when possible\n- Use specific column names instead of SELECT *\n- Consider using JOINs for related data\n- Add WHERE clauses to filter data when needed\n\n## Important Notes\n- The OpenEdX MySQL datasource is already configured and ready to use\n- You can create multiple panels with different queries in the same dashboard\n- Remember to refresh your panels periodically to see updated data",
              "mode": "markdown"
            },
